# Ceraa secrets template — copy to a non-tracked location and fill in.
# Used by ceraa.service (EnvironmentFile=/etc/ceraa/ceraa.env)
# and by run-ceraa.sh / start-bot.sh / start-daemon.sh.
#
# There is deliberately no default provider. Ceraa ships with no URL, model, or
# key baked in, so on first run it asks which provider to use and stores the
# answer per provider. Set these only if you want to pre-seed a provider from
# the environment instead of choosing in Telegram.

# Telegram bot token from @BotFather
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# Allowlisted Telegram user/chat ID
TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USER_ID=

# Optional: pre-seed an OpenAI-compatible provider instead of using Telegram
# onboarding. Leave blank to choose a provider in Telegram.
CERAA_API_URL=
CERAA_MODEL=
CERAA_API_KEY=

# Where the bot should run
HOME=/home/assistant

# The Mini App surface is on by default. It serves on loopback and reaches the
# internet through a Cloudflare tunnel rather than a published port, and every
# data route requires a signed initData and an exact user-id match.
#
# A bot token on its own is a complete install: nothing here has to be set, the
# surface comes up at boot, the menu button is rewritten whenever the tunnel
# changes hostname, and a client that dies is replaced within two minutes.
#
# Set both of these to turn it off, on a host that should publish nothing.
#

# The tunnel is a separate switch on purpose.
# With CERAA_MINIAPP=0 and the tunnel
# on, nothing is published; with the surface on and the tunnel off, the Mini App
# is reachable only from this machine.
#
# BotFather's "Main App" is a different field, set only through BotFather, and
# this does not touch it. Leave it disabled unless the URL is one you control.
# CERAA_MINIAPP=0
# CERAA_MINIAPP_TUNNEL=0

# Passive memory extractor. At compaction, Ceraa runs one small, cheap LLM call
# over the discarded head of the session and stores only high-confidence
# durable preferences. It is off (no API key needed for anything else) unless a
# key is set here; the defaults point at a low-cost poolside endpoint. The
# extractor writes directly to the memory store, so the loop flows without a
# human approving each item - a short "learned N, contradicted M" footer is
# emitted instead. Remove the key to disable it, or override the endpoint and
# model below.
CERAA_EXTRACT_URL=https://inference.poolside.ai/v1
CERAA_EXTRACT_MODEL=poolside/laguna-s-2.1
# CERAA_EXTRACT_KEY=

# Memory delivery mode. Default is "cached": a bounded, ranked memory block is
# rendered into the stable prefix of every prompt so preferences are visible on
# every turn at cache-hit cost. Override with "prompt" to put the block in the
# tail (uncached every turn, the old behaviour), or "sidekick" to annotate tool
# results only and leave the prompt fully static.
# CERAA_MEMORY_DELIVERY=cached
